# .gitignore for the NL2FRET repository
# Principle: the tool (nl2fret_tool/) and the project documents are tracked. experiments/ (run records, inputs, results) is excluded except the entries
# listed as exceptions below; the tool's own run output (nl2fret_tool/runs/) is excluded by nl2fret_tool/.gitignore.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual environments (experiments/nl2fret/.venv is 1.2 GB and contains hard-coded absolute paths, so it is not tracked)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Operating system and editor files
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*secret*
*credentials*

# Temporary working directories (FRET check work files, 812 generated NuSMV .smv inputs, etc.)
work/
tmp/
.mock_state/
results_mock/


# Archives (input and result zips; the result folders also exist unpacked)
*.zip

# LaTeX build artifacts (generic; docs/paper/ is already excluded as a whole below)
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.synctex.gz

# Docker cache
.docker/

# Exclusions decided by the project owner (2026-11-08): local instructions, experiment records, and the paper in progress
testnote.md
docs/records/UNVERIFIED.md
experiments/*
docs/paper/

# Exceptions inside experiments/ (2026-11-17). `experiments/` itself must not be ignored (a file cannot be re-included when its parent folder is ignored), so the
# pattern above ignores the entries of the folder and these lines take three of them back:
#   ltlpack/            the NuSMV and Spot comparison study (it was tracked as packages/ltlpack before it moved into experiments/)
#   000_INDEX.md        numbering of the experiment folders and the experiment folder rule
#   RESULTS_INDEX.md    index of the result folders
# Files inside ltlpack/ that match another pattern of this file (*.zip, work/, __pycache__/) stay ignored, as before.
!experiments/ltlpack/
!experiments/000_INDEX.md
!experiments/RESULTS_INDEX.md

# Added 2026-11-11 at the project owner's request: survey notes of the cleanup, and files whose purpose could not be determined
# (A .gitignore entry does not affect files that are already tracked; see STRUCTURE.md section 4c.)
docs/refactor_plan/
nl2fret_tool/archive/unsorted/

# ---- Open items (whether to track them is for the project owner to decide) ----
# 1. Large result folders: experiments/nl7/results_lm (about 67 MB), experiments/nl3/results_nl3 (about 36 MB), etc.
#    They are tracked at present. If size becomes a problem, uncomment the next line to exclude only large raw
#    outputs such as calls.jsonl.
# experiments/**/calls.jsonl
# 2. The 11 paper PDFs (experiments/nl2fret/pdfs, about 25 MB) are covered by the experiments/ exclusion. The paper in
#    progress (docs/paper/) is excluded as a whole.
# 3. Run logs (run.log, console.log, *_console.log) are run records and are kept tracked.
# 4. Because *.zip is excluded, the original input archives (inputs/*.zip) are not in git. Store them elsewhere
#    if they must be preserved.
# 5. Because the entries of experiments/ are excluded (except the exceptions above), items 1 to 3 above (tracking of results
#    inside the experiment folders) do not currently apply.
